A||||54||filthyscarecrow||what's the fastest car you've ever driven? ||||1||
Z||000000||filthyscarecrow||04-06-2001||03:05 AM||||and please don't say your fiero. if your fiero is the fastest thing you've ever driven, then, my friend, there is a whole world of fine machinery out there for you to discover. i guarantee i haven't driven the fastest car in terms of acceleration, but a formula 2000 is pretty quick in the corners (1.3g). the U of M formula SAE car accelerates at 1.3g, corners at a constant 1.3g with a 1.9g transient g max. the traction circle is about 50% bigger than a viper's. but my dad's friend has a porsche 911 GT1-R that i've got my eye on. 800hp GT-1 race car. but i'll probably never get to drive that one, although he said he's plannign on putting a passenger seat in it and giving rides. <BR>yeeeeeeeeeee haaaaaaaaaaaa. <BR>so what have you flogged? <P>------------------<BR>allow me to show you my exhaust pipes...||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-06-2001||07:45 AM||||my old 92 tbird Nascar stock car. on the race track of course. hehe. on the street a toss up I think between my Valiant convert with 426 hemi and a friends 454 powered Countach replica. Ive had my Fiero up to around 175. just not as quick as the other 2.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-06-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||hugh||04-06-2001||07:52 AM||||On the street,my family car.1987 Grand National.On the track,my dragster. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||04-06-2001||08:46 AM||||the fastest car Ive ever drove was a Yugo, it had a quad turbo, twin dual cam, 6 liter, aluminum, ported and polished, V12 producing 953 hp and 952 tq. It accelerated from 0-60 mph in 2 seconds, while blasting the 1/4 in 9 secs at 142 mph.<P>or ummmmm, maybe not, lol. most likely the fasest would be a new vette but I would still like to drive the before mentioned yugo!<P> <BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/formula_sig_yeehawbw.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||MrPBody||04-06-2001||09:14 AM||||I know you guys can top this, but . . .<P>The fastest <I>car</I> I've driven was a neighbor's Aston Martin DB4, but I didn't drive it very fast.<P>The fastest <I>I</I> have driven was about 120 in my old Jag 3.8 Mk II.<P>The fastest I have <I>ridden</I> was about 140 in a buddy's hemi Roadrunner.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||04-06-2001||09:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by hugh:<BR><B>On the street,my family car.1987 Grand National.On the track,my dragster. </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Fun car!  I had one back in '87.  My first brand new car.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>The fasted car I've ever driven was my '72 Trans Am, 455HO - bone stock.  I had it up to about 140 once and it was rock stable.  With an overdrive, there's no telling how fast that sucker would go.<P>On the flip side, the slowest "vehicle" I've ever driven:  The Shuttle Crawler Transporter!  Top speed, about 2mph, but I never got it over about 1.5.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||04-06-2001||10:47 AM||||I hear that crawler is a bear to park....<P>Fastest Car Ive Driven...1967 Camaro Convertible powered by 350ci with all kinds of extra goodies.  It could burn the tires through first gear and then bark'em again in 2nd and 3rd.  It was just plain bad a$$.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<P>"Who wants somma Debo?"||||reg||1
Z||000007||fierogt88||04-06-2001||10:56 AM||||I didn't get to drive it, but I rode in danny boy's stealth twin turbo last night and was very VERY impressed.  There was a topic on here a while back about stealth's not being impressive, but let me tell you, I was freakin scared more than once. 0-90 so fast i had to hold onto the door handle (oh $h!t handle).  You'd have to have an LT1 or better and a hell of a lot of improvement to the suspension to get a fiero to compare.||||reg||1
Z||000008||stimpy||04-06-2001||02:06 PM||||Probably the fastest car I've <B>driven</B> has been my Mazda 323 GTX. Sad to say I haven't driven that many ultra-fast cars. I've ridden in some rockets. I think the most impressive was a BMW 745i Alpina that a neighbor gave me a ride in. That thing scooted, but felt like it was doing the speed limit at 100mph. The opposite of that smoothness would have to be the Pantera my dad had when I was in High School. That was nastyscaryfast. ||||reg||1
Z||000009||KRMFiero||04-06-2001||02:25 PM||||Not leagly but my friends '91 Eclipse N/A  that thing hauls @$$... If i remember right i was doing like 75 in 3rd gear and it wasnt fully redlined, i had it up to about 130 that day  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> (on long road, no one goes on, very wide road to hehe)||||reg||1
