Z||000019||Songman||04-07-2001||12:10 AM||||Probably my fastest car was my 911 Targa. I only took it to 120 but it had plenty left. In my younger days, when I would buy a sports car and get it broken in good I would give it the '120 test' just to say I had done it. Now I have no desire to drive that fast. It is just stupid and dangerous unless you are on a closed course somewhere.<P>Others that made that club... Jag XJS-HE V12 and C-4 Corvette. I know my V8 Lexus LS400 would do it but no need to prove it to myself...heheh<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000020||danny boy||04-07-2001||12:11 AM|||| Gotta be my '70 Nova SS as far as quickest. 10.73 1/4 mile and I drove the damn thing on the street. My dad built it in his teenage years and gave it to me for my 17th Bday. 355, 4sp muncie, 3:73 rear. It is now sitting in a garage under covered because I am nowhere near responsible enough to drive it.<BR> Fastest? Probably the Stealth.||||reg||1
Z||000021||Oreif||04-07-2001||12:27 AM||||Rode in:<BR>My fathers 1969 GTO with the Royal Bobcat kit. (Mom had it up to 120mph on a highway while we were on vacation, she claims she didn't know she was going that fast!)<P>Drove:<BR>Lotus Esprit Turbo, I actually took it for a test drive! (in 1987)<P>Fastest speed in a car:<BR>1973 Trans AM with the 455SD<BR>Speedo went up to 160 we had it at 145. Had to slow down the rear tires were leaving the ground on the crest of the hills.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||AkursedX||04-07-2001||12:47 AM||||The fastest cars I've driven have been an Acura NSX, and Lotus Espirt Turbo.  I didn't get to really open them up though.  My friends' father owned both of them and let me taken them for a spin a couple times  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>The Fastest I have driven was 151 mph in my father's 1994 Chevy Caprice.  It was an old police car, and my father rebuilt the engine and made some mods to it.  Man do I miss that car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  ||||reg||7
Z||000023||Songman||04-07-2001||01:21 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Oreif:<BR>[B]Rode in:<BR>My fathers 1969 GTO with the Royal Bobcat kit. (Mom had it up to 120mph on a highway while we were on vacation, she claims she didn't know she was going that fast!)<BR>[B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Wow! A real Royal Bobcat! I have never even seen on except in pictures! I sold my Ram Air IV 69 Judge last year. It was pretty fast, but bottom end not top. It's somewhere up there in your area now, Oreif. A dealer from Chicago bought it.<P><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000024||Oreif||04-07-2001||01:24 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Songman:<BR><B> Wow! A real Royal Bobcat! I have never even seen on except in pictures! I sold my Ram Air IV 69 Judge last year. It was pretty fast, but bottom end not top. It's somewhere up there in your area now, Oreif. A dealer from Chicago bought it.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Was the last name "Sullivan"? I know he has been collecting lots of cars over the years. He has one of eight made 1969 Trans Am convertables. A friend works at the dealership and aided in the restoration of the T/A.<P><BR>BTW ~ My Fathers GTO was stolen in 1973 and recovered by the police in 1977. The only thing left was the shell and frame.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000025||Songman||04-07-2001||03:53 AM||||I'm not sure what the guys name was. I sold my car to a buddy of mine to buy my 87 Aerocoupe. He turned it around to the guy up there.<P>I also sold my 69 Firebird convertible last year. I was going to do a T/A clone out of it if I kept it. Only I was gonna do pearl white with  metallic blue stripes. From a distance it would look the same but you would know when you got close. I have an original RA III 400 engine that I was gonna put in it. I'm a Pontiac man at heart!<P>This is a picture of the two of the above mentioned cars. This is the day I bought the Judge. This is my buddy's wrecker lot down in GA where I store some of my cars. You can see some of the other GTOs in the background.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.com/tnfieros/pontiacs.jpg">  <P>Bummer about your dad's car. Some things just can't be replaced.<BR>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
