Z||000033||Raydar||04-08-2001||11:06 AM||||Fastest car I've ever ridden in is probably a 69 Mach I with a 428 CJ. Friend of mine had it for only a few weeks before he got busted for 100 mph in a 35 and DUI. Flew past a cop that was sitting at a stopsign on a side street.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> <BR>On another occasion, he claimed to have had the speedo "wrapped around between the blinkers". (This would have translated to about 140. On a two lane road.) <BR>Glad I wasn't with him for either of these excursions.<BR>Fastest I've ever driven was probably in my 350 Monza. Don't know how fast I was going, but I "out-nerved" a Porsche 911 driver on I-85. Pretty sure he just backed off, though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>Another time (also on I-85), a guy in a GTI kept passing me, tucking in in front of me, then slowing down. After about the second time, I pulled around him and stomped it until he was a speck in the mirror. <BR>Not sure how fast I was actually going. Was a long time ago. I'm guessing maybe 120. NOT a real big deal. Unless I woulda got caught or hit something.   <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
