Z||000037||Rex||04-08-2001||10:27 PM||||In 1975 I had my 70-AMX to 130 mph. The valves were floating and I perceived the brakes went out on decerleration.Come to find out I was airborne.The car had average modifications 360 cid, w/ram air and automatic. When I touched down and got stopped I removed my underwear and tossed them over the hill.  LOL  thanks for the memories||||reg||1
Z||000038||2birds||04-08-2001||11:45 PM||||Fastest I've driven was my 94 Thunderbird Super Coupe.  100 mph all day long, and a couple of 125 mph bursts just for fun.  All along the old Montanabahn.  Not bad for a family car... <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I've touched 120 a few times in the Fiero , too.<P>My 94 Mustang GT is going to get me busted real quick.  I was testing out the transmission separator plate mods I recently did, and it did the 2-3 shift at around 85 mph before I realized how fast I was going.<BR>  ||||reg||1
